WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 5.5 · Internal Systems & Operations
People and HR systems overview

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
People systems start with your founders' agreement and grow with each person who joins.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
People systems cover the whole journey of everyone who works with you, paid or unpaid, from planning the team to leaving. Even with only founders, your founders' agreement is the first piece.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
What to decide now

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:40.463
People records: Where records are kept and who can see them, with tighter access than working files. For example: The bakery keeps each trainee's file in a folder only the two founders can open.

6
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:51.422
Leave and absence: How holidays, sickness and other absence are recorded and covered. For example: The bakery founders log holidays in one shared calendar, so someone always covers the ovens.

7
00:00:51.422 --> 00:01:05.433
Pay and documents: How pay will run once you have paid people, and what each person must read and sign. For example: The bakery uses an external payroll service from the trainees' very first payday.

8
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:06.433
Why set it up now

9
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:11.367
1. Personal records need protecting from the very first volunteer.

10
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:16.300
2. Contracts and payroll are required with your first employee.

11
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:22.604
3. A simple version now is easier than fixing gaps later.

12
00:01:23.004 --> 00:01:23.604
What it connects to

13
00:01:23.604 --> 00:01:29.278
1. Module 4: how to design each part of the people journey.

14
00:01:29.278 --> 00:01:33.841
2. Your information system: access levels for personal records.

15
00:01:33.841 --> 00:01:38.293
3. Your joining and leaving checklists.

16
00:01:38.693 --> 00:01:39.293
What to avoid

17
00:01:39.293 --> 00:01:44.596
Keeping personal records in ordinary shared folders or group chats.

18
00:01:44.596 --> 00:01:49.530
Waiting for the first employee to think about payroll.

19
00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:54.722
Not checking the rules where you are.

20
00:01:55.322 --> 00:01:57.122
You describe your people systems and who can access each.

21
00:01:57.122 --> 00:02:01.122
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.722
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
